From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:49:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] power: supply: iceland-supervooc: end the automatic
 session at 85 %

The owner's charge rule ends charging at 85 %; the automatic stage ended at 90 %.
Only the end of charge changes; the current ladder, the voltage ends and every
thermal guard stay as in the driver.

Based on dappermint/iceland-supervooc commit 614469fabe59 ("ci: run the host tests on every push");
builds on DocZ13's SC8547D handover in iceland-linux issue #2 and on OnePlus's open-source oplus_chg code.

Link: https://github.com/dappermint/iceland-supervooc

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/vooc_logic.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/vooc_logic.h b/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/vooc_logic.h
index 67a50527d39b7..3926f6c08d9c9 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/vooc_logic.h
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/vooc_logic.h
@@ -1179,7 +1179,7 @@ static inline void vl3_ladder_pump(const struct vl3_io *io, struct vl3_lad *l, i
 #define V4_SETTLE_READS		30		/* reads after an ask change: the adapter takes a new ask only through the change code and then ramps, so the
 						 * taper does not count and the total limit keeps the old ask until then */
 #define V4_END_MV		4480		/* a single gauge read above it ends the session (stock's first step-down voltage) */
-#define V4_END_SOC		90
+#define V4_END_SOC		85	/* iceland: the owner's 85 % end (dappermint: 90) */
 #define V4_REARM_MS		30000		/* offline is believed this long after a session's end (the firmware's own unsuspend dips VBUS) */
 #define V4_RECHECK_MS		60000		/* a start refused before any write: the gates are read again this long after the refusal */
 #define V4_NO_LIMIT		0x7fffffff
@@ -1279,7 +1279,7 @@ static inline const char *vl4_why(int c)
 {
 	switch (c) {
 	case V4E_VOLT:	return "battery voltage above 4480 mV";
-	case V4E_SOC:	return "complete: 90 %";
+	case V4E_SOC:	return "complete: 85 %";
 	case V4E_FLOOR:	return "complete: taper reached 2.0 A";
 	}
 	return "?";
-- 
